---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const faqs = [["What is the difference between testing and enforce mode?", "Testing mode reports TLS failures without affecting delivery. Enforce mode requires valid TLS and bounces connections that do not support it."], ["Does Cloudflare Email Routing support MTA-STS?", "Yes, Cloudflare Email Routing supports STARTTLS. Publishing an MTA-STS policy in enforce mode requires that all MX hosts support TLS."]];

const article = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Article',
  headline: "MTA-STS Record",
  description: "MTA-STS record: enforce TLS for email delivery via DNS TXT record and HTTPS-hosted policy file. RFC 8460.",
  inLanguage: 'en',
  author: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'PromptDNS', url: 'https://promptdns.com/' },
  publisher: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'PromptDNS', url: 'https://promptdns.com/', logo: { '@type': 'ImageObject', url: 'https://promptdns.com/favicon.svg' } },
  datePublished: '2026-10-27',
  dateModified: '2026-10-27',
};

const faqSchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'FAQPage',
  mainEntity: faqs.map(([q, a]) => ({
    '@type': 'Question',
    name: q,
    acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: a },
  })),
};

const breadcrumbs = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
  itemListElement: [
    { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Home', item: 'https://promptdns.com/' },
    { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'Email Authentication', item: 'https://promptdns.com/email-authentication/' },
    { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 3, name: "MTA-STS Record" },
  ],
};
---
<BaseLayout
  title="MTA-STS Record: Enforce TLS for Email Delivery via DNS and HTTPS Policy"
  description="MTA-STS record: enforce TLS for email delivery via DNS TXT record and HTTPS-hosted policy file. RFC 8460."
  schema={[article, faqSchema, breadcrumbs]}
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 py-12">
    <nav class="mb-4 text-sm text-ink-faint" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/" class="hover:text-accent">Home</a>
      <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <a href="/email-authentication/" class="hover:text-accent">Email Authentication</a>
      <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <span class="text-ink-dim">MTA-STS Record</span>
    </nav>
    <h1 class="font-display text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-ink sm:text-4xl">MTA-STS Record</h1>
    <p class="mt-4 text-lg text-ink-dim">MTA-STS record: enforce TLS for email delivery via DNS TXT and HTTPS policy file. RFC 8460.</p>

    <section class="not-prose my-8" aria-label="Reference table">
      <div class="glass rounded-2xl p-5 shadow-lg sm:p-7 overflow-x-auto">
        <table class='pdns-table' style='width:100%'><thead><tr><th class='whitespace-nowrap'>Component</th><th class='whitespace-nowrap'>Location</th><th class='whitespace-nowrap'>Purpose</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='pd-mono'>DNS TXT record</td><td>_smtp._tls.domain.com</td><td>Signals MTA-STS support: v=STS1</td></tr><tr><td class='pd-mono'>HTTPS policy file</td><td>https://mta-sts.domain.com/.well-known/mta-sts.txt</td><td>Defines TLS policy: mode, max_age, MX hosts</td></tr><tr><td class='pd-mono'>DNS TXT record (TLS-RPT)</td><td>_smtp._tls.domain.com (separate record)</td><td>Reporting address for TLS failures: v=TLSRPTv1; rua=...</td></tr></tbody></table>
      </div>
    </section>

    <article class="rich-text mt-10 max-w-none">
      <h2>Technical details</h2>
      <p class='mt-3'>An MTA-STS (SMTP Mail Transfer Agent Strict Transport Security) record is a DNS TXT record published at _smtp._tls.domain.com that signals a domain's support for TLS-enforced email delivery, as defined in RFC 8460.</p><p class='mt-3'>The MTA-STS policy file is hosted at https://mta-sts.domain.com/.well-known/mta-sts.txt and defines the enforcement mode (none, testing, or enforce), the maximum policy age, and the list of expected MX hosts.</p><p class='mt-3'>MTA-STS prevents downgrade attacks where an attacker strips the STARTTLS encryption from SMTP connections, forcing email to be transmitted in plaintext.</p>

      <aside class="mt-8 rounded-xl border-l-3 border-l-violet/50 bg-violet/5 p-5" aria-label="Practitioner field notes">
        <p class="font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-violet mb-2">Field notes</p>
        <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim italic">MTA-STS is the easiest TLS enforcement mechanism to deploy (compared to DANE) because it uses HTTPS rather than DNSSEC. The policy file must be served over HTTPS with a valid certificate for mta-sts.domain.com.</p>
      </aside>

      <h2 class="font-display mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Frequently asked questions</h2>
      <div class="mt-3 grid gap-3">
        <details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">What is the difference between testing and enforce mode?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">Testing mode reports TLS failures without affecting delivery. Enforce mode requires valid TLS and bounces connections that do not support it.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">Does Cloudflare Email Routing support MTA-STS?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">Yes, Cloudflare Email Routing supports STARTTLS. Publishing an MTA-STS policy in enforce mode requires that all MX hosts support TLS.</p></details>
      </div>

      <p class="mt-8 text-xs text-ink-faint">
        Check your domain with our free tools:
        <a href="/spf-record-checker/" class="text-accent hover:text-accent-soft">SPF checker</a>,
        <a href="/dmarc-record-checker/" class="text-accent hover:text-accent-soft">DMARC checker</a>,
        <a href="/dkim-record-checker/" class="text-accent hover:text-accent-soft">DKIM checker</a>.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
